L394: - Two PhD students with doctoral fellowships
L395: _Responsible for information related to nutrition:_
L396: - Clinical nutrition physiologist, PhD student Ingrid Løvold Mostad, Clinical Services, St.
L397: Olavs Hospital, Trondheim
L398: _Exercise groups:_ 2 physiotherapists at St. Olavs Hospital, 1 physiotherapist at Levanger
L399: Hospital, 1 physiotherapists at Ålesund Hospital
L400: **Feasability**
L401: In both national and international literature the importance of physical activity are
L402: highlighted. WHO has recently presented a global strategy for nutrition, physical activity and
L403: health (Sosial- og helsedepartementet, 2004). In Norway physical activity and exercise have
L404: been strongly addressed, and is an issue of high priority also in pregnant and postpartum
L405: women (St.meld.nr.16, Handlingsplan for fysisk aktivitet). Nevertheless, few trials evaluating
L406: the effects of regular exercise have been published. The present trial aims at answering some
L407: questions related to the effects of regular exercise in a very important group, that is pregnant
L408: women.
L409: Intervention trials including exercise programs are complicated, and needs close follow up of
L410: the participants. However, this research group has previously carried through several similar
L411: RCT’s in women during pregnancy and after delivery (see publication lists).
